      cleanupNote.innerHTML = `<b style="color:${colors.text};"><i class="fas fa-broom" style="color:${colors.primary || '#38bdf8'};"></i> Smart cleanup</b><br>Use this for scroll-heavy pages: the monitor can lazy-mark media, drop far-offscreen media sources, apply content-visibility, and optionally hibernate far-offscreen card DOM into restoreable tombstones. The pressure ladder chooses the lightest rung from observe → soft → burst → smart so small scroll jumps do not pay for heavy cleanup. DOM budget sweep is the absolute guard: it watches live DOM/media/heap budgets even when no new burst happens, then runs the selected relief rung. Hibernation is stronger than containment because it reduces live DOM nodes, but keep it manual until you confirm the site restores cleanly.`;
